    justification:  # d53b
    description: "Merge tree view and DataTable into a single 'Integrated View' (possibly a third mode alongside flat table and tree toggle). Key design decisions from human discussion:\n\n1. **New view mode, not replacement.** Add an \"Integrated View\" as a third option. If it works well, make it the default.\n\n2. **Constrained manual ordering (</>).** In integrated view:\n   - Child items cannot be positioned above their parent\n   - Children can be reordered among siblings\n   - Moving a parent moves its entire subtree as a unit\n   - One-member families (no parent, no children) are treated as standalone units\n   - A one-member family cannot be positioned between members of another family; it skips the whole family as a unit\n   - Items in multi-member families cannot be moved outside their family via </> — use 'p' hotkey to re-parent first\n\n3. **Filter interaction with parents.** If a filter would hide a parent but its children are visible, show the parent anyway with all row text italicized (never bolded). This preserves hierarchy context.\n\n4. **Ghost rows.** Ghost rows (hidden chain members) stay at table bottom, not inserted at tree position. Simpler to implement and reason about for the # column.\n\n5. **Two competing axes concern.** Flat priority view and hierarchy view serve different purposes. Integrated view prioritizes hierarchy; users who want pure flat ordering use the existing table mode."  # d53b
    fields: {}  # d53b
